        <profile name="Ancient Collector" id="43bd-24bc-a3d6-08e0" hidden="false" page="85" publicationId="61c6-c8c5-pubN65537" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">If this model is included in your army, the Dynastic Heirlooms Strategem costs 1 fewer Command points to use the first time you use it. If this model is included in your Crusade force, the Relic Requisition costs 0 Requisition Points to use.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile name="Surrogate Hosts" id="c25e-90dd-705c-bb59" hidden="false" page="85" publicationId="61c6-c8c5-pubN65537" typeId="72c5eafc-75bf-4ed9-b425-78009f1efe82" typeName="Abilities">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="21befb24-fc85-4f52-a745-64b2e48f8228">When this model is destroyed, instead of using any other rule that is triggered when a model is destroyed, after removing it from play you can roll one D6; on a 2+, you can select another friendly NECRONS INFANTRY CHARACTER model on the battlefield (excluding named characters). Remove that model as if it were destroyed (you cannot use any rules that are triggered when a model is destroyed) and return this model to play, placing it in the removed model&apos;s place with 3 wounds remaining.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
